{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1126918-qarinah-2-0","id":1126918,"title":"Qarinah 2.0","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-09T18:45:40-07:00","id":1126918,"title":"Qarinah 2.0","content":"Okay I think my former idea really only clicked for one person so I have a new idea for Qarinah. <br /> <br /> The Qarinah are creatures of the Abyss, that have been reverse corrupted by the Fallen world thanks to the rituals of a sorceror who summons them into thr world. <br /> <br /> As such thier summomer is both their strength amd their weakness as thier summoner can only be a mere mortal. <br /> <br /> In fact the Summoner IS there power stat, but that benifits the Summoner very little directly, it just means they are better at the rituals that summon, feed, and empower you.<br /> <br /> What changed you from being a regular horror of the Abyss, was the sacrifice made by the Summoner, to make something that has no right to exist into something truely real, to take an antisymbol and make it a symbol, something real has to be sacrificed, to be made unreal, so that the Quarinah can take its place in reality.<br /> <br /> During the ritual of Quarinah summoning, the Summoner offers someone they are connected to as a sacrifice, someone mortal, although the Sacrifice need not be present as long as the Summoner has something of theirs.<br /> <br /> If the Sacrifice fails to resist the Abyss accepts the offer, and swallows that poor person, devouring them, and the new Qarinah appears in the Summoning circle.<br /> <br /> Power Stat: Summoner, the higher the Summoner level, the more power the Summoner can feed into you from the Abyss, and the better the Summoner gets at the rituals that benifit and empower you and the more rituals they know. All Summoners start with the Summoning, Banishing, and Feeding Rituals. Summoners are mortal and if your Summoner dies, you are cast back into the Abyss, likely forever.<br /> <br /> At higher Summoner you can choose benifitial Rituals for your Summoner to learn, like rituals that allow you to heal yourself by commiting certain acts, but at Summoner 6+ you become valueible to unique baleful rituals. Summoner always knows these rituals they you &quot;gain&quot; them, but they can be learned by others.<br /> <br /> Mortality Stat: Partnership, 1-10, your relationship with your Summoner, 1 being the Master in your relationship, and 10 being Slave (like Harmony, both ends have penalties and benifits), do you gloriously rule or lovingly serve?<br /> <br /> Powers: Antisymbols and Rituals, Antisymbols are your magical abilities (like contracts, disciplines, gifts, and so on), and Rituals are the magical rites your Summoner learns to interact and empower you (or in rare cases punish you like Banish).<br /> <br /> Example rituals are feed (the Summoner sacrifices something to the Abyss into order for you regain fuel stat), Protection from Bleeding (the Qarinah takes reduced damage from sharp weapons when the Summoner does a Ritual and Sacrifices a knife to thr Abyss, extra benifit if it has great personal or fincial value). Protection from Mages (the Summoner completes the Ritual and Sacrifices their own ability to withstand Supernal Spells in order to increase it for the Qarinah for the duration).<br /> <br /> Fuel Stat: Taint, the Qarinah has three ways of gaining Taint, 1 the ritual of feeding cast by their Summoner, 2 spending time back in the Abyss, and 3 <br /> draining the life force from semen (in the Midevil sense of semen, which both men and women were concidered to possess, in practice sexually draining the fertility of ones partner/s, the more taint the Qarinah gains the longer the sexual partner is sterile for).<br /> <br /> Taint can be spent on powering Antisymbols, making the Qarianah fertile for a time (more on Qarinah and what they can do with fertility), healing their Summoner (has unfortunate side effects), healing ones self, reading surface emotions, shapeshifting, communicating with the Gods of the Abyss while in the Fallen World or sending a messags to your Summoner over a distance.<br /> <br /> Shapeshifting: You can the shape of the Sacrificed mortal that was used to Summon you, your natural form, which cost no taint to shift between, but for a point of taint, you can take the form of someone's sexual fantasies that you are touching or whose emotions you are reading.<br /> <br /> Qarinah Fertility: Qarinah have no natural fertility, but Taint can be used to make a Qarinah fertile in ways not supposable for humans. 1 point of taint can allow the Qarinah to have a child with a human, leading to a human child. 2 points of Taint can allow the Qarinah to haveva child with another type of Monster as if the Qarinah was human. For 3 Taint the Qarinagh can have a child with a Abyssal God, allowing the Qarinah to give birth to something truely monsterous (Gulmoth or Acamoth, maybe something more horrifying) that obeys its parents commands for a time.<br /> <br /> Antisymbols: The Qarinah makes an antsymbol in the air and reality bleeds for a brief moment in that shape, only to unleash its effect. The Qarinah unleashes the Antisymbol of Calitrex and the targets leg breaks, thanks to an accident that never happened, call upon the Antisymbol of Shnax and the targets lungs fill with a substance that has never existed for example.<br /> <br /> Mages and Qarinah: compared to Mages and Qarinah, Beasts and Demons are BFF. Most Mages concider Qarinah abominations that have no right to exist, surviving thanks to the damntion of an innocent mortal, and Qarinah concider Mages hypocrits that seem to have no problem twisting supernal symbols in unnatural ways.Those that use Abyssal magic instead simply try and use the Qarinah. <br /> <br /> Qarinah don't hate reality like other Abyssal creatures, the rituals of their Summoner have made her more then antisymbol and has granted them a place in the fallen world, a piece of reality to call their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T20:25:07-07:00","id":1126943,"title":"","content":"It's extremely chill that the dimensional hell monsters have sex powers and gain fuel by recharging their J/O crystal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T07:22:39-07:00","id":1127097,"title":"","content":"Yeah, with all the Horrors and other supernaturals that have succubus-like traits, I wouldn't have thought succubi/incubi would be metaphysical untruths","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T08:04:49-07:00","id":1127123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1126918-qarinah-2-0?p=1127097#post1127097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, with all the Horrors and other supernaturals that have succubus-like traits, I wouldn't have thought succubi/incubi would be metaphysical untruths</div> </div> </div> </div> They're former untruths, that's the thing, the first Summoning ritual trades the truth of a mortal human to the Abyss which grants most of that truth to one of its antisymbols, so the Qarinah is a semi truth, trapped somewhere between symbol and antisymbol, but not truely either. <br /> <br /> They are from the Abyss, but they are no longer truely apart of the Abyss, banishing them back to the Abyss even for a time is unpleasant for them, as they no longer really fit in there anymore.<br /> <br /> I thinking the Y and X splats should Parent Akkunai (Abyssal Realm) and Hedonies, the organizations the Qarinah have made for themselves.<br /> <br /> The Hedonies are: The Sinful (proudly indulges in vices, likes to party), The Repentant (feels bad for the Sacrifice, wishes to find a way to restore them without damning themselves), The Faithful (religiously worship the Gods of the Abyss), The Transcendant (goal is to become Supernal Creatures like Cherubs), The Responsible (wants a balanced life, very practical).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}